    },
    {
      "post_id": "93791",
      "author_handle": "MollyUK",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 7 months 6 days ago",
      "body": "We’ve done London a couple of times with kids and the main thing I’d say is look for somewhere with a bit of space rather than a standard hotel room - it makes a huge difference with three children.\nAparthotels or family rooms tend to work really well so you’re not all squeezed in.\nLocation-wise, somewhere central but slightly quieter (like around South Bank or near Kensington) can be a good balance - easy to get around but not too hectic at night.\nAlso worth checking if they include breakfast - saves a lot of hassle in the mornings with kids.",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-9544/#93791",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/f96e40bf9e5584983564.html",
      "page_url": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-9544/",
      "role": "response",
      "original_post_id": "85006"
    }
